"Two soluble models of an antiferromagnetic chain for Annals of Physics - IBM Research (https://research.ibm.com/publications/two-soluble-models-of-an-antiferromagnetic-chain)\nciteturn78view0 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://research.ibm.com/publications/two-soluble-models-of-an-antiferromagnetic-chain\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 74\nL0: cite0†Annals of Physics L1: \nL2: Paper\nL3: \nL4: 01 Jan 1961\nL5: \nL6: # Two soluble models of an antiferromagnetic chain\nL7: \nL8: cite1†View publication†dx.doi.org L9: ## Abstract\nL10: Two genuinely quantum mechanical models for an antiferromagnetic linear chain with nearest neighbor interactions are constructed and solved exactly, in the sense that the ground state, all the elementary excitations and the free energy are found. A general formalism for calculating the instantaneous correlation between any two spins is developed and applied to the investigation of short- and long-range order.\nL11: Both models show nonvanishing long-range order in the ground state for a range of values of a certain parameter λ which is analogous to an anisotropy parameter in the Heisenberg model. A detailed comparison with the Heisenberg model suggests that the latter has no long-range order in the isotropic case but finite long-range order for any finite amount of anisotropy. The unreliability of variational methods for determining long-range order is emphasized.\nL12: It is also shown that for spin 1 2 systems having rather general isotropic Heisenberg interactions favoring an antiferromagnetic ordering, the ground state is nondegenerate and there is no energy gap above the ground state in the energy spectrum of the total system. © 1961.\nL13: ## Related\nL14: \nL15: Paper\nL16: \nL17: ### cite2†New method in the theory of imperfect gases and liquids L18: \nL19: Elliott Lieb\nL20: \nL21: Journal of Mathematical Physics\nL22: \nL23: Paper\nL24: \nL25: ### cite3†Ordering energy levels of interacting spin systems L26: \nL27: Elliott Lieb, Daniel Mattis\nL28: \nL29: Journal of Mathematical Physics\nL30: \nL31: Paper\nL32: \nL33: ### cite3†Ordering energy levels of interacting spin systems L34: \nL35: Elliott Lieb, Daniel Mattis\nL36: \nL37: Journal of Mathematical Physics\nL38: \nL39: Paper\nL40: ### cite4†Theory of ferromagnetism and the ordering of electronic energy levels L41: \nL42: Elliott Lieb, Daniel Mattis\nL43: \nL44: Physical Review\nL45: \nL46: cite5†View all publications L47: \nL48:   1. cite6†Home L49:   2. ↳ cite5†Publications L50: \nL51: ## Date\nL52: \nL53: 01 Jan 1961\nL54: \nL55: ## Publication\nL56: \nL57: cite0†Annals of Physics L58: \nL59: ## Authors\nL60: \nL61:   * cite7†Elliott Lieb L62:   * cite8†Theodore Schultz L63:   * cite9†Daniel Mattis L64: \nL65: IBM-affiliated at time of publication\nL66: \nL67: ## Resources\nL68: \nL69:   * cite1†Publication†dx.doi.org L70: \nL71: ## Share\nL72: \nL73:   *   *   *\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n[1104.1721] Exact ground state of the sine-square deformed XY spin chain (https://arxiv.org/abs/1104.1721)\nciteturn78view1 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: today; Content type: text/html; Source: open({\"ref_id\":\"https://arxiv.org/abs/1104.1721\",\"lineno\":null}); Total lines: 169\nL0: cite0†Search cite1†Submit cite2†Donate†info.arxiv.org cite3†Log in L1: \nL2: Search arXiv [Input: Search papers by title, author, abstract, or ID...] [Input] [Input]\nL3: \nL4: Press Enter to search · cite4†Advanced search L5: \nL6: # Condensed Matter > Statistical Mechanics\nL7: \nL8: [Submitted on 9 Apr 2011 (cite5†v1 ), last revised 15 May 2011 (this version, v2)]\nL9: # Title:Exact ground state of the sine-square deformed XY spin chain\nL10: \nL11: Authors:cite6†Hosho Katsura L12: \nL13: View a PDF of the paper titled Exact ground state of the sine-square deformed XY spin chain, by Hosho Katsura\nL14: \nL15: cite7†View PDF cite8†HTML (experimental) L16: > Abstract:We study the sine-square deformed quantum XY chain with open boundary conditions, in which the interaction strength at the position $x$ in the chain of length $L$ is proportional to the function $f_x = \\sin^2 [\\pi/L (x-1/2)]$. The model can be mapped onto a free spinless fermion model with site-dependent hopping amplitudes and on-site potentials via the Jordan-Wigner transformation.\nL17: Although the single-particle eigenstates of this system cannot be obtained in closed form, it is shown that the many-body ground state is identical to that of the uniform XY chain with periodic boundary conditions. This proves a conjecture of Hikihara and Nishino [Hikihara T and Nishino T 2011 {\\it Phys. Rev. B} \\textbf{83} 060414(R)] based on numerical evidence.\nL18: Comments:  | 10 pages\nL19: Subjects:  | Statistical Mechanics (cond-mat.stat-mech); Strongly Correlated Electrons (cond-mat.str-el); Quantum Physics (quant-ph)\nL20: Cite as:  | cite9†arXiv:1104.1721 [cond-mat.stat-mech]\nL21:    | (or cite10†arXiv:1104.1721v2 [cond-mat.stat-mech] for this version)\nL22:    | cite11†https://doi.org/10.48550/arXiv.1104.1721†doi.org arXiv-issued DOI via DataCite\nL23: Journal reference:  | J. Phys. A: Math. Theor. 44 (2011) 252001\nL24: Related DOI (Digital Object Identifier):  | cite12†https://doi.org/10.1088/1751-8113/44/25/252001†doi.org DOI(s) linking to related resources\nL25: ## Submission history\nL26: \nL27: From: Hosho Katsura [cite13†view email ]\nL28: cite5†[v1] Sat, 9 Apr 2011 16:35:31 UTC (11 KB)\nL29: [v2] Sun, 15 May 2011 12:53:51 UTC (11 KB)\nL30: \nL31: Full-text links:\nL32: \nL33: ## Access Paper:\nL34: \nL35: View a PDF of the paper titled Exact ground state of the sine-square deformed XY spin chain, by Hosho Katsura\nL36: \nL37:   * cite7†View PDF L38:   * cite8†HTML (experimental) L39:   * cite14†TeX Source L40: \nL41: cite15†view license L42: ##